WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.620
Report a fault as a work order with its priority, place and technician, so nothing gets forgotten.

2
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:14.370
Maintenance shows every open job in the mall, and which ones are late.

3
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:21.020
Open work orders, how many are urgent, and how many are past their agreed time.

4
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.050
Most urgent lists what to do first: emergencies at the top.

5
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:33.330
Choose New work order. Tenants' requests from their portal arrive here by themselves.

6
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:39.090
Say what is wrong, in a few words.

7
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.960
The trade: it decides who is told.

8
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:49.210
The priority. Each one has its own time to respond and to fix.

9
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:57.200
Where it is: a unit, an asset, or a place in the common area.

10
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.510
What you saw and what was already done.

11
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.560
Choose the technician now, or leave it for the supervisor.

12
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:14.790
Raise the work order. The technician is told at once, and the clocks start.

13
00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:20.260
These two timers show the time left to respond and to fix.
